# Cubit and State Files Coupling

> **Enforced by:** manual review (no reliable automated check)

**Rule:** Use `part` and `part of` to link Cubit and State files together instead of regular imports. The Cubit file should declare `part 'feature_state.dart';` and house all the necessary imports, while the State file should declare `part of 'feature_cubit.dart';` and should not have any imports of its own.

**State equality:** State classes extend `Equatable` and list every field in `props`, so emitting a state equal to the current one is skipped (no redundant rebuilds) and tests compare states by value. Import `package:equatable/equatable.dart` in the Cubit file — the State file has no imports.

### ✅ Good Example
```dart
// In feature_cubit.dart
import 'package:equatable/equatable.dart';
import 'package:flutter_bloc/flutter_bloc.dart';
import 'package:flutter_production_starter/domain/entity/user_entity.dart';

part 'feature_state.dart';

class FeatureCubit extends Cubit<FeatureState> { ... }

// In feature_state.dart
part of 'feature_cubit.dart';

class FeatureState extends Equatable {
  final UserEntity? user;
  ...
  @override
  List<Object?> get props => [user];
}
```

### ❌ Bad Example
```dart
// In feature_cubit.dart
import 'package:flutter_bloc/flutter_bloc.dart';
import 'feature_state.dart';

class FeatureCubit extends Cubit<FeatureState> { ... }

// In feature_state.dart
import '../../../domain/entity/user_entity.dart';

class FeatureState { ... }
```
